    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Here are the essential commands for navigating folders in Terminal:\n\n- **`cd <path>`** — Change directory (e.g., `cd Documents`, `cd ..` to go up one level, `cd ~` to go home)\n- **`pwd`** — Print working directory (shows where you are)\n- **`ls`** — List files and folders in the current directory\n- **`cd -`** — Go back to the previous directory\n\nQuick examples:\n```bash\ncd /home/user/Documents   # absolute path\ncd ../..                  # go up two levels\ncd ~/Projects             # ~ expands to home directory\n```",
     "time": {
      "start": 1789689323543,
      "end": 1789689323981
