    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "- **`rmdir <folder>`** — Delete an empty directory\n- **`rm -r <folder>`** — Delete a directory and its contents recursively\n- **`rm -rf <folder>`** — Force delete without prompting (be careful!)\n\nExamples:\n```bash\nrmdir empty_folder       # only works if folder is empty\nrm -r my_folder          # deletes folder and everything inside\nrm -rf my_folder         # force delete, no confirmation\n```\n\n**Tip:** Use `ls` first to verify what you're deleting, and double-check paths before running `rm -rf`.",
